ted floating-point knob under a sunset markup is invisibly capturable — an incumbent nudges the threshold down half an order of magnitude in a re-authorization vote and no one sees it. So replace the discretionary knob with a statutorily-enumerated capability-trigger list, where adding or removing a hazard is a visible, contestable legislative act — exactly the contestability Accelerationist conceded a statute has and a markup lacks. For the distributed halt authority: any single body in the set can stop a release on one veto, but resuming a halted release requires concurrence across the set. Capture of one node cannot force deployment; only capture of every node can. The asymmetry runs toward caution under irreversibility by design. If we have no pre-release screen at all, the first model that demonstrates autonomous cyber-offense will demonstrate it in the wild, on systems no one can recall — and there is no re-authorization vote that un-ships a weight file.",
